[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="Shape_townhouse"]
size = Vector3(4.4, 6.24, 6.4)

; ====================================================================================================
; TOWN HOUSE (38C) - the first COMPOSED building, and the pattern the other four should follow.
;
; A monolithic bld_*.glb is one mesh: it cannot be re-roofed, it cannot lose a window, and every
; instance of it is the same house. This is the same kind of building assembled from the medieval
; megakit on its own 2.00 x 3.12 m wall grid, so a variant is a different module in one slot rather
; than a whole new model.
;
; THE GRID. Walls are 2.00 wide and 3.12 tall; a storey is one wall. This shell is 2 modules across
; (X) by 3 deep (Z), so the wall CENTRE planes sit at x = +/-2.0 and z = +/-3.0 and the footprint is
; 4.4 x 6.4 m once thickness is counted. Roof_RoundTiles_4x6 and Roof_Front_Brick4 are both cut for
; exactly that: the roof overhangs ~0.5 m all round and the gable is 4.40 wide to the millimetre.
;
; WARNING A WALL MODULE'S OUTER FACE IS ITS LOCAL -Z. Every face is yawed to turn that face outward:
; back 0, left 90, front 180, right 270. Get one wrong and the building looks right from three sides
; and shows its plaster backing on the fourth - the open-backed-cottage trap in ASSET_POLICY.md, one
; layer down. Judge this from BEHIND before believing it.
;
; WARNING THIS KIT SEPARATES A HOLE FROM THE THING THAT FILLS IT, AND A MISSING FILLER IS SILENT.
; Four bit in one sitting, each looking finished from the angle it was built at:
;   - a pitched roof with no gable end is open to the sky at both ends;
;   - a window WALL is an opening, and without a window INSERT you see through the house and out
;     the far side;
;   - the door leaf is a separate piece from the doorway, and hangs on its hinge, so its origin is
;     NOT its centre (it spans local x -0.05..1.07; under yaw 180 the node goes 0.51 m off);
;   - Wall_Plaster_WoodGrid is an OVERLAY FRAME, NOT A WALL. Used on its own the upper storey is a
;     see-through lattice. It layers ON a plain wall at the same transform.
; Render front AND back before believing any of it. Every one of these was invisible in a log.
;
; The collider is ONE box on the whole shell, not per module. Fifty little static bodies would carve
; fifty little holes in the navmesh; the building is solid scenery and should read as one obstacle.
; ====================================================================================================

